      "answer": "Based on the evidence, MapleBridge does not look like a one-off. The same Canada-specific approval-rule failure pattern shows up in at least these other customers in the evidence: MapleFork Franchise Systems, MapleWest Bank, and MapleBay Marketplace [art_6376b15b1c33] [art_ad58f3ce1afd] [art_364eddbcbfe8] [art_39c1434aa40a].\n\nCustomers and what happened:\n- MapleBridge Insurance: after the 2026-03-12 migration, about 117 approvals bypassed the Canada approver because the rules engine used the wrong rule during a schema/version propagation lag and conflicting priority between canada.v2 and global.v3 [art_6376b15b1c33]\n- MapleFork Franchise Systems: their recovery playbook explicitly fixes precedence so region overrides win over global defaults for Canada-ON and Canada-QC approval flows [art_ad58f3ce1afd]\n- MapleWest Bank: after migration, mixed predicates and renamed fields caused missing keys to be treated as falsy, which let the global-default rule match instead of the Canada-specific path [art_364eddbcbfe8]\n- MapleBay Marketplace: after migration, approvals with country=CA were intermittently stuck or auto-denied because the compiled ruleset put the global-default at priority 1000 ahead of the country override at priority 900 [art_39c1434aa40a]\n\nPlain-English shared failure pattern:\nAfter a migration or rule change, the system picked the wrong approval rule for Canada. The Canada-specific override lost to a global/default rule, or schema/sync/metadata issues caused the engine to evaluate the global rule instead of the Canada rule, leading to bypassed, denied, or blocked approvals [art_6376b15b1c33] [art_ad58f3ce1afd] [art_364eddbcbfe8] [art_39c1434aa40a].\n\nWhat I can\u2019t prove from this evidence:\n- whether this is a true recurring pattern across all Canada accounts\n- a definitive population-wide count or exhaustive list of all Canada accounts with this failure pattern",
